206324,20424,2,0.13,0.082,[[26,0.5,2,1],[8,0.5,20,1]],[],0,128],[7202587,20424,512,9.607,7.821,[[26,0.954,3,491],[7,0.039,46,18],[13,0.008,9,3]],[["8e1f001e_6270c83d",70,-1,0,"Is there a reason we're creating these new methods instead of using e.g. onViewWaiting(withText(...))"],["a225ee9e_8bcd0973",70,-1,0,"ditto here: can we use onView(withText(...))?"],["ccbf592e_60c993b4",70,-1,1,"nit: We can add `>` to the items that show a nested menu to make them visually distinguishable."],["cfd75e76_0ad1163e",46,-1,1,"Is this only used for testing? If so, maybe name it setDrillDownOverrideValueForTesting and add ResettersForTesting.register(() -> mDrillDownOverrideValue = null);"]],0,129],[7206712,20424,78,2.024,1.5,[[26,4]],[],0,130],[7206075,20424,135,3.9,2.8,[[26,5]],[],0,131],[7151638,20425,140,4.21,3.407,[[0,46]],[["65c8830a_0c81f32c",71,-8,1,"`std::make_unique` is a more safe alternative."],["a45da99b_086e12e3",72,-8,1,"nit: Do we use this header?"],["c8f758e2_ddd17843",72,-8,1,"Can you add comments to the class?"],["197f34a9_be740026",73,-2,1,"Do we wanna keep this todo? Since we are restructuring the extensions toolbar, I'm ok with dropping it. We can later add TODOs if we think it could be improved"],["3dfa9f6b_4a62e30b",74,-2,1,"I know this comment is copied from extensions_toolbar_container, but I think it can be dropped because: - `ToolbarActionsBar` no longer exists - pbos no longer works on chromium - we are now handling…"],["ba8047e9_a573ffd9",71,-2,1,"nit: lets specify the type since it's not clear what `RemoveAction` returns."],["f21bd369_2a994f4b",24,-2,1,"ETCVM will be platform-agnostic. Lets move thi to `enable_extension_core` so its included on Desktop Android. Same for the .cc"]],0,132],[7234895,20431,11,0.421,0.3,[[0,47]],[],0,133],[7240507,20432,40,1.341,1.058,[[0,1.0,48,168]],[],0,134],[7262336,20441,220,4.21,3.407,[[0,49]],[["b10478c8_018ae190",73,-2,1,"nit-optional: I would name this toolbar_model or toolbar_view_model, to avoid confusion with other potential view models"]],0,135],[7235730,20444,263,7.601,6.192,[[0,50]],[["8811042e_bcc39534",74,-14,1,"Not for this CL: naming is getting quite long. What about dropping `container` from the name? It doesn't add much.. Final naming could be - ETCVW -> `ExtensionsToolbarViewModel` - ETC ->…"],["afb2b215_9d2b465d",74,-14,1,"I was going to suggest to not have a method in the delegate, and instead pass the action delegate from ETC to the ETCVM However, once we finish the whole refactor the observers for \"on action added\"…"],["c304e5f3_e807f629",74,-14,1,"From 'Extensions UI Architecture for Desktop Android' [doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/13M2nTvVBy4kr01u6-54zw1YkpdLJXsoe8z72lhy6cKE/edit?usp=sharing) and CL comments for the extensions menu…"],["256fdb6c_c9c25e6a",72,-13,1,"Let's introduce an Observer instead for these methods, with names like `OnAction{Added,Removed}`. See crrev.com/c/7165256 for a similar CL for EAVM, and also the comment thread with Emilia at…"],["744ddcc5_642466dd",75,-12,1,"I'm not a fan of having three ways the ETVC and ETC to \"communicate\": (1) Delegate, for ETVC getting information from ETC (2) Observer, for ETVC notifying changes to ETC (3) ETC calling ETVC methods,…"],["4ba368f1_be9e7ba4",71,-11,1,"This \"helps\" `ExtensionsToolbarViewModel` correctly handle the case where `ToolbarActionsModel` was initialized before its construction, but it should be handled by `ExtensionsToolbarViewModel`…"],["6b1f68c9_aae986cd",76,-11,1,"When this method is called, this should always hold. So it should rather be `CHECK()`."],["72da5d62_f7ba7a0f",71,-11,1,"nit: You can use `ScopedObservation` for better safety."],["cc71eef2_5e847150",76,-11,1,"Why do we need this? Is not clear to me why adding an observer to ETVM also means adding one to TAM"],["10d41c3c_8d2caf49",75,-10,1,"Lets change the comment to reflect what this class is for, rather than what it does: ``` Delegate used to retrieve platform-specific information. ```"],["164bbb71_3dbc1e14",75,-10,1,"nit: I would name this `CreateActionDelegate` since it's the delegate for the action"],["36094bc5_7bc74c87",75,-10,1,"nit: same here -> `actions_model_observation_`. When I was first reading the .cc file, thought it was an observation to this class, which was confusing"],["6f474171_f09c10d1",76,-10,0,"I know this is a copy from [1], but it's not clear what it's doing. We should add some comments. Taking a step back. When do we need to reorder? - If action is added, we need to add to the correct…"],["7ff60f85_a6dddd48",75,-10,1,"nit: ``` Observer used to notify platforms about changes to the model. ```"],["8e5591b4_04e23573",71,-10,0,"separate cl: lets rename this to be `GetActionModel(action_id)` so it reflects that is returning the model"],["97304821_9752764a",76,-10,1,"I know this is a copy from [1], but it's not clear what it's doing. We should add comments. However, taking a step back. When do we need to reorder? How are we keeping track of the order? Is actions_…"],["9a905691_07878a6d",75,-10,1,"Some of these comments have a verb (e.g 'creates', 'removes'), but usually observer methods comments are descriptive of the event. For example: ``` // Called when an action is added to the model. ```"],["bb5ee5a6_a7c37820",75,-10,1,"nit: add comments"],["ef44e323_c2c4a690",71,-10,1,"nit: the name `Icon` is not really used. Lets use `ActionView` since that's the terminology we are using"],["f8d2f4d6_ba3d1a7a",75,-10,1,"nit: I would name this `actions_model_`, so it's more clear what its the model for. (we have various delegate, models..)"],["974d24d0_cb5ac967",75,-7,1,"Is this TODO no longer relevant?"],["56f68bfd_b607380c",76,-5,0,"Let's use `CHECK` consistently. I recently learned that `CHECK` is now recommended in Chromium for invariants/contracts."],["84311d4c_ff777213",71,-5,1,"I think it's safer to keep the contract check: ``` CHECK(icons_.empty()); ```"],["c4398f12_a305ee8f",76,-5,0,"nit: Do we need explicit `Reset`? I think the default destructor does it for you."],["73f14a44_59cc1899",75,-4,1,"nit: comment ``` // The delegate to retrieve platform-specific information. const raw_ptr<Delegate> delegate_; // The observers that handles platform-specific UI. base::ObserverList<Observer>…"],["e097d19e_08bbf704",76,-4,1,"idea: What if instead we have: ``` actions_.push_back(delegate_->CreateActionViewModel(action_id))); ``` then we can leave the platform specific construction at the platform level. That is,…"],["16d76206_d3040ea0",71,-3,1,"It's a bit confusing to call `OnActionsInitialized()` here because the model might not be initialized yet. I recommend either: 1. introduce a getter method in the view model class to check if the…"],["8cc62122_2b0fb445",75,-3,1,"I recommend keeping `observers_` here (after all ctor-initialized members) to ensure correct destruction order."]],0,136],[7231426,20444,125,2.361,1.866,[[0,51]],[],0,137],[7276943,20445,115,2.361,1.866,[[0,52]],[],0,138],[7300005,20445,100,2.361,1.866,[[0,1.0,53,722]],[["b69127f8_adf55340",5,-1,1,"Please fix this WARNING reported by Spellchecker: \"occurances\" is a possible misspelling of \"occurrences\". To bypass Spellchecker... \"occurances\" is a possible misspelling of \"occurrences\". To bypass…"]],0,139],[7300025,20445,96,2.361,1.866,[[0,1.0,54,232]],[],0,140],[7268066,20445,88,2.361,1.866,[[0,55]],[["f97315e2_8b14c9be",75,-4,0,"IIUC `index` here refers to an index of *pinned* actions, so owner classes need to know whether each action is pinned or not and count the number of pinned actions to the left of the dragged actions.…"],["fa9d196e_1853e02d",76,-1,1,"nit: We could add comments to make this more clear ``` // Find the action's current index and verify it is currently pinned. auto iter = .. CHECK ... int current_index ... // Calculate the target…"]],0,141],[7299504,20445,124,2.361,1.866,[[0,56]],[["d5e52fb2_4a30f1b3",77,0,1,"What do we use this for?"]],0,142],[7307809,20448,16,0.737,0.556,[[0,57]],[["bb628417_33ccb768",76,-3,1,"nit: optimization, reserve memory to avoid reallocations during the loop. ``` initial_actions.reserve(action_ids.size()); ```"]],0,143],[7317109,20449,94,2.113,1.57,[[4,0.735,38,70],[12,0.245,4,23],[3,0.02,1,1]],[],0,144]]}